scenario ser-pivot-before-in-ends
title "Serializable: the middle transaction is aborted before the first one ends"
story "T1 to T2 to T3, with T3 committing first and T1 still open when T2 commits. This engine aborts T2 as soon as T3 commits. PostgreSQL lets T2 commit, then T1 rolls back by itself and nobody is aborted. If T1 commits instead, PostgreSQL aborts T1, not T2. Why PostgreSQL decides at that point is not established."
schedule:
  T1 BEGIN
  T3 BEGIN
  T2 BEGIN
  T1 READ q:1 AS v1_0
  T2 SCAN p: AS v2_2
  T2 PUT p:3 = 75
  T3 PUT p:2 = 48
  T1 SCAN p: AS v1_2
  T1 PUT q:1 = 63
  T3 COMMIT
  T2 COMMIT
  T1 ABORT
